{
  "_comment": [
    "Pronunciation metadata for the English audio tracks. §13: 'Pronunciation is metadata, never",
    "different words.' Nothing in this file changes a single character of what is printed on the",
    "page - it only tells the voice how to say what is already there.",
    "",
    "Two forms are given for every entry, on purpose:",
    "  ipa  - fed to Azure as <phoneme alphabet='ipa'>. Uses the en-GB/en-IE/en-AU phone set, which",
    "         is the set Azure publishes for the British-family English locales. en-NZ is NOT in",
    "         Azure's published phone-set table, so if it rejects these the pipeline falls back to",
    "         the 'say' form automatically. See scripts/audio.mjs.",
    "  say  - a plain respelling. Doubles as the fallback (<sub alias>) AND as the column a curator",
    "         reads, because almost nobody can proofread IPA.",
    "",
    "System: traditional English pronunciation of scientific Latin - the one used by English-speaking",
    "biologists, not Classical or Church Latin. Stress falls on the penultimate syllable when it is",
    "heavy, otherwise the antepenultimate. Initial ps-, pt-, cn-, ct-, gn-, mn- drop the first letter.",
    "Final -es is 'eez', final -e is 'ee', ae/oe are 'ee', c and g before e/i/y are soft.",
    "",
    "confidence: high   - rule-derived, standard, and I would ship it.",
    "            medium - a real variant exists and biologists differ; either is defensible.",
    "            low    - genuinely unsure, usually an eponym whose owner's name drives the sound.",
    "                     Every 'low' needs a human answer before it ships.",
    "",
    "Eponyms are the trap: a genus named after a person follows the PERSON's name, not Latin rules.",
    "Peachia is PEECH-ee-a because Charles Peach was PEECH, and no amount of Latin gets you there."
  ],

  "alphabet": "ipa",
  "locale": "en-NZ",
  "phoneSet": "en-GB/en-IE/en-AU",

  "reviewed": true,
  "reviewedBy": "David Brouwers",
  "reviewedOn": "2026-08-14",
  "_reviewNote": [
    "All 161 entries approved as they stand, including the seventeen marked low confidence.",
    "The confidence and why fields are kept rather than cleared: they record WHY each reading was",
    "chosen, which is what a future reviewer needs in order to disagree with it. Approval means",
    "these ship, not that the reasoning stopped being worth reading.",
    "",
    "Still worth a Museum answer at some point, though nothing is blocked on it: Blaschka is a",
    "German family name printed on every object and on the front of the app, and the family's own",
    "pronunciation is the kind of thing an institution can simply ask about."
  ],

