  "_epithetsComment": [
    "105 distinct species epithets appear in the catalogue titles. Most are ordinary Latin",
    "adjectives - australis, borealis, vulgaris, marina, rubra - that an English voice handles",
    "acceptably without help, so they are deliberately left alone. Marking up everything makes the",
    "narration worse, not better, and buries the entries that matter.",
    "",
    "Listed here are only the ones a voice reliably gets wrong: eponyms ending -ii or -i, where the",
    "sound follows a person's name, and words whose consonant clusters have no English analogue.",
    "The remainder need a listening pass, not a lexicon entry - see docs/audio-pipeline.md."
  ],

